# Opinion

Meeting: 0003-improve-the-design-and-aesthetics-of-rps-arena
Agent: Developer
Task: Improve the design and aesthetics of RPS Arena
Context:
- Implemented a design refresh for the SPA: new sticky top bar with active nav states, hero stat grid, richer hero card, and updated panels/cards styling with gradients and focus affordances.
- Added `public/viewUtils.js` with pure render helpers (news, leaderboard, highscores, match history, status messages) and rewired `public/main.js` to use them for sanitized, testable markup.
- Expanded CSS tokens, typography (Space Grotesk), and responsive layouts; kept all functionality buildless and API-compatible.
- Augmented tests with `tests/uiRender.test.js` covering every view helper branch to maintain c8 global 100% coverage.

Position:
- Keep front-end logic modular by separating data fetch from rendering; sanitize all UI output to guard against injection and improve reliability.
- Prefer CSS variables and lightweight gradients/glass effects over additional JS interactions; focus on clarity for form feedback and list readability.

Recommendations:
- When extending UI further (e.g., queue polling), keep helper functions pure and covered; update tests alongside to protect branch coverage expectations.
- Maintain nav state management in `main.js` and avoid introducing routing—panels + active buttons remain sufficient for SPA navigation.
- Continue serving assets directly from `public/` to align with the current Node static handler; no bundler required unless scope changes.
